<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Policarpo Bonilla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1926">1926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Policarpo Bonilla was a Honduran lawyer and Liberal politician who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-of-honduras">Liberal Party of Honduras</a> in 1891 and was president from 1894 to 1899, after taking power with Nicaraguan help. His government adopted a liberal constitution in 1894, and with the presidents of Nicaragua and El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> he formed the Greater Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/policarpo-bonilla.jpg" alt="Policarpo Bonilla" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harper's new Monthly magazine 1855 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Policarpo_Bonilla_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
